.TH SOND 1 "2026-07" "Sond" "Sond Language Manual"
.SH NAME
sond \- a programming language optimized for verifiability in the AI era
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Sond
is a language written by AI and used by AI. Its aim is a language in which it is
.I almost impossible
to make a programming or logic error: extremely hard for a human to write, yet
extraordinarily hard for an AI to be wrong. Every function may carry a contract
.RB ( requires / ensures );
the compiler
.BR sondc (1)
.I proves
those contracts at compile time and rejects any it cannot verify, so a wrong body
does not compile.
.PP
Sond programs are written in
.I .snd
files and compiled with
.BR sondc (1)
to hosted executables, freestanding kernels, UEFI applications, or C\-ABI shared
objects. There is no interpreter; the artifact is native x86\-64.
.SH LANGUAGE REFERENCE
The complete, current reference \(em the one document needed to write correct Sond \(em
is
.IR Sond.md ,
installed at
.IR ~/.local/share/sond/Sond.md .
Point an AI model or an editor at it.
.SH USAGE
.nf
sondc hello.snd -o hello   # compile
./hello                     # run (exit code = the entry function's value)
.fi
.SH USING SOND AS A TOOLCHAIN
.B tools/install.sh
installs Sond like a self\-contained toolchain (in the spirit of Go's
.B go
+
.BR GOROOT ):
.BR sondc (1)
onto
.IR PATH ,
the standard library as a versioned copy at
.IR ~/.local/lib/sond/ ,
and this reference at
.IR ~/.local/share/sond/Sond.md .
An external project then depends on the installed Sond, not on the compiler's
source tree, and includes standard\-library modules by their canonical path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sondc (1)
